RefundExpired_Concrete_Test
├── given the refund is switched off
│   └── it should revert
└── given the refund is switched on
    ├── when the batch is empty or holds more than 100 ids
    │   └── it should revert
    └── when the batch holds 1 to 100 ids
        ├── when an id was never opened
        │   └── it should revert
        └── when every id was opened
            ├── given a position has already ended
            │   ├── it should skip it
            │   └── it should refund the rest of the batch
            └── given the positions are open
                ├── when the delay has not passed since the expiry of a position
                │   └── it should revert
                └── when the delay has passed since the expiry of every open position
                    ├── when a payout has too little gas
                    │   └── it should revert
                    └── when every payout has the gas it needs
                        ├── given the token refuses a payout
                        │   ├── it should keep the stake for the user to claim
                        │   └── it should refund the rest of the batch
                        └── given the token pays
                            ├── it should return each stake to its user, with no fee
                            ├── it should release each position's hold on the pool and leave free money unchanged
                            ├── it should close each position
                            ├── it should emit {PositionRefunded} for each, before its payout
                            └── it should return the number refunded
